    "model_design": "WHAT: Upgrade TabularFeatureInteractionNet to accept both continuous feature vectors and discrete categorical indices, utilizing dedicated nn.Embedding layers for discrete identifiers alongside continuous FeatureTokenizer projections. WHY: Treating discrete community district and building class codes as continuous numbers introduces artificial euclidean distance; dedicated embedding tables allow the transformer self-attention layers to learn realistic spatial clusters and property risk phenotypes. HOW: Modify TabularFeatureInteractionNet.__init__ to instantiate nn.ModuleList with nn.Embedding for borough, CD, and building class (projected to embed_dim=32); in forward(x_cont, x_cat), concatenate categorical embedding tokens, continuous feature tokens, and the CLS token into the transformer sequence before passing through self-attention and the wide highway skip connection. INTERFACE CONSTRAINTS: Maintain build_model(num_cont_features, cat_cardinalities, embed_dim=32, ...) and keep AsymmetricFocalLoss and build_optimizer interface signatures consistent.",
    "training_evaluation": "WHAT: Implement multi-cohort training data pooling by loading and extracting features for the 2020-01-01 cutoff (PLUTO 19v2, target window 2020-2021) and concatenating it with the 2021-01-01 cutoff (PLUTO 20v7), expanding training volume from ~171k to ~340k samples while keeping 2022 validation untouched. WHY: Training on a single annual cohort caused AP saturation by epoch 10; multi-cohort pooling exposes the transformer to diverse multi-year inspection cycles and provides sufficient sample diversity to train categorical embeddings without overfitting. HOW: In the execution pipeline, load PLUTO 19v2 to build the 2020 cohort, concatenate with the 2021 cohort to form train_features, fit StandardScaler strictly on continuous columns, construct TensorDataset with (X_cont, X_cat, y), and execute the training loop with OneCycleLR scheduler and best AP checkpointing. INTERFACE CONSTRAINTS: Preserve validation on the 2022 cutoff evaluated with average_precision_score, and generate submission/submission.csv with columns ['bbl', 'score']."
